# VMaxxing Scheduled Research — crontab template (Route A)
# =================================================================
#
# This file provides ready-to-use crontab entries that call
# ``vmx -p "<prompt>"`` on a schedule. Each line runs a
# separate one-shot research task; the results are written to
# ``agent/runs/`` just like a normal interactive run.
#
# INSTALL:
#   1. Copy the lines you want into your crontab:
#        crontab -e
#   2. Replace <AGENT_DIR> with the absolute path to your vmx
#      agent directory (e.g. /Users/tianle/Desktop/VMaxxing/agent).
#   3. Replace <PYTHON> with your Python binary path.
#   4. Adjust the prompts and schedules to your needs.
#
# ADVANCED (recommended):
#   For full lifecycle management (add/list/pause/resume/delete jobs,
#   persistent store, crash recovery, email notifications), use the
#   ``watch`` daemon instead:
#       export VIBE_TRADING_ENABLE_SCHEDULER=1
#       vmx watch
#   Then manage jobs with:
#       vmx schedule add <id> <prompt> <schedule>
#       vmx schedule list
#
# SCHEDULE REFERENCE (crontab format):
#   minute  hour  day-of-month  month  day-of-week  command
#   *       *     *             *      *            (every minute)
#   0       9     *             *      1            (Monday 9am)
#   30      16    *             *      1-5          (Weekdays 4:30pm)
#   0       */6   *             *      *            (Every 6 hours)
#   */30    *     *             *      *            (Every 30 minutes)
#
# =================================================================

AGENT_DIR=<AGENT_DIR>
PYTHON=<PYTHON>

# --- Example 1: Weekly sector scan every Monday at 9:00 AM ---
# Scans a sector and writes a research memo.
# 0 9 * * 1 cd $AGENT_DIR && $PYTHON -m cli -p "Scan the semiconductor sector: find top 5 momentum stocks, analyze recent earnings, and flag any unusual volume activity. Write a concise weekly scan report." --no-rich

# --- Example 2: Daily after-close momentum scan (Mon-Fri 4:30 PM) ---
# 30 16 * * 1-5 cd $AGENT_DIR && $PYTHON -m cli -p "Run a daily momentum scan on S&P 500: identify stocks with RSI(14) crossing above 50, 20-day SMA breakout, and above-average volume. Rank by momentum score." --no-rich

# --- Example 3: Hourly anomaly detection ---
# 0 * * * * cd $AGENT_DIR && $PYTHON -m cli -p "Check for market anomalies in the last hour: unusual volume spikes (>3x average), price gaps >2%, and sudden volatility changes in major indices." --no-rich

# --- Example 4: Every 30 minutes price alert check ---
# */30 * * * * cd $AGENT_DIR && $PYTHON -m cli -p "Check if any stocks in my watchlist (AAPL, NVDA, TSLA, MSFT, GOOGL) have moved more than 2% in the last 30 minutes. Flag any breakouts or breakdowns." --no-rich

# --- Example 5: Weekend portfolio review (Sunday 6:00 PM) ---
# 0 18 * * 0 cd $AGENT_DIR && $PYTHON -m cli -p "Generate a weekly portfolio review: summarize major market events, review key positions, calculate portfolio performance metrics, and suggest rebalancing actions for next week." --no-rich

# --- Example 6: Pre-market briefing (Mon-Fri 8:30 AM) ---
# 30 8 * * 1-5 cd $AGENT_DIR && $PYTHON -m cli -p "Pre-market briefing: summarize overnight futures movement, check pre-market gainers/losers, review any after-hours earnings reports, and highlight key economic events for the day." --no-rich

# =================================================================
# LOGGING (optional but recommended)
#
# Append ``>> /tmp/vmx-cron.log 2>&1`` to capture output:
#
# 0 9 * * 1 cd $AGENT_DIR && $PYTHON -m cli -p "Scan..." --no-rich >> /tmp/vmx-cron.log 2>&1
#
# TIP: Use ``--json`` instead of ``--no-rich`` for machine-readable output
# that can be piped into downstream tooling (Slack, email, database, etc.).
# =================================================================
